## Red work

I adopted and finished the two interrupted worker Red tests. The lifecycle suite
checks typed registration, startup bounds, bounded polling, concurrency,
readiness, liveness, SIGTERM drain, safe logs, safe failure fields, and the
least-privilege lifecycle port.

The architecture suite checks the named composition root, DB and schema imports,
SQL and job-table references, backend port imports, and exact adapter-root
persistence ownership.

The import guard also rejects relative imports into `packages/db` and
`packages/backend`, while allowing only `@reading-advantage/backend/jobs`.
The persistence guard scans TypeScript and SQL files under the backend jobs root.

